## 4. Output

### 4.1 Topology Structure
Topology link information is stored in the `Topo` structure. The array variable `aj_link` stores each link [source node ID, destination node ID, weight, bandwidth, latency]. All links are directed.

```cpp
struct Topo {
    int16_t aj_link[1000][5];                           // Link information array
    uint32_t link_num;                                  // Number of links
    
    uint32_t net_npu_num;                              // Number of network NPUs
    uint32_t sw_num;                                   // Number of switches

    int16_t port_num[MAX_SW_NUM + MAX_NET_NPU_NUM];    // Port numbers per node
    int16_t next_hop_port[MAX_ALL_PORT_NUM];           // Next hop port mapping
    uint32_t sw_port_num;                              // Switch port count
    uint32_t net_npu_port_num;                         // Network NPU port count

    Topo() : aj_link{}, link_num(0), net_npu_num(0), sw_num(0), port_num{}, next_hop_port{} {}
};
```

### 4.2 Forwarding Information Base (FIB)
The routing table is stored in the `Fib` structure. The `next_hop_num` field is currently unused.

```cpp
struct Fib {
    int16_t fib[MAX_SW_NUM + MAX_NET_NPU_NUM][MAX_NET_NPU_NUM][MAX_ONE_SW_PORT_NUM];
    int16_t next_hop_num[MAX_SW_NUM*MAX_ONE_SW_PORT_NUM + MAX_NET_NPU_NUM*2];
    
    Fib() {
        std::memset(fib, 0, sizeof(fib));
        std::memset(next_hop_num, 0, sizeof(next_hop_num));
    }
};
```

